  "notes": "Title: 'VP 12/12 Voltage converter'. Pins are drawn in joined pairs: two pin stubs (upper and lower number) meet in a dot on one outside line. Pairs: 1+24 (labelled 5V), 12+13 (GND), 11+14 (+), 10+15 (-), 3+22 (+), 2+23 (-). The + and - signs are inside the box beside each right-hand pair; 'inside' is put on the upper pin of each pair. The upper pin of each pair is a bent line that turns down to the join; the join dot is a mark."
